 "src": "Flipkart SDE OA",
 "body": "<p>A grid has <code>R</code> rows and <code>C</code> columns, and each cell holds some goods. Robot 1 starts at the top-left cell and robot 2 at the top-right cell.</p><p>Every step, both robots move down one row at the same time. Each moves to the cell below-left, directly below or below-right, and must stay inside the grid. A robot collects the goods of every cell it visits. If both robots are on the same cell, its goods are counted once.</p><p>Print the maximum total the two robots can collect after reaching the bottom row.</p><h3>Function to complete</h3><p>Complete <code>maxGoods(grid)</code>. It returns the maximum goods collected.</p><p class=\"muted\">Input reading and printing are handled for you, like on LeetCode. The input format below is what the tests and <i>Custom input</i> use.</p>",
 "inp": "The first line contains <code>R</code> and <code>C</code>. Each of the next <code>R</code> lines contains <code>C</code> integers.",
 "out": "One integer: the maximum goods collected.",
 "cons": [
  "1 ≤ R, C ≤ 50",
  "0 ≤ goods ≤ 100"
 ],
